WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:22.540
[Background music ]

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:30.719
[Narrator:] It's time to quit for the day.
The afternoon has worn itself out. In a short

00:00:30.719 --> 00:00:33.030
while now, it will be dark.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:38.730
Yes, it's time to let the cotton and tobacco
go. Time to get the mules and horses, time

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:46.770
to milk the cows if you keep cows, time to
quit work and head for home. Time for supper.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.360
[Sound of banging on a pan with a ladle.]

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:51.760
[Woman:] Come and get it.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:57.220
[Narrator:] Come and get it, iced tea, corn
pones and grits, turnip greens, pork chops maybe.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:01.620
It's been a long day and stomachs are
empty.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:12.800
Now supper is over and it's evening time and
this is the time we want to talk about. Our

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:19.039
story is about the time of day when it's getting
dark and cool, about resting time.

00:01:19.039 --> 00:01:26.219
[Man singing song.]

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:33.600
Yes, this is resting time. A time to sit quietly
and talk and play some music and sing a little

00:01:34.459 --> 00:01:40.409
if you've got a voice for things, but resting
time is a danger time too.

00:01:40.409 --> 00:01:47.409
The hours that come after dark are dangerous
hours. Mosquito hours from dark to dawn, the

00:01:47.779 --> 00:01:52.329
malaria-carrying mosquitoes search for food
and they bite people who are sleeping or sitting

00:01:52.329 --> 00:01:56.069
quietly or moving only a little.

00:01:56.069 --> 00:02:02.039
The cool hours of early dark are dangerous.
This is a time when the mosquitoes do their work.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:10.259
At this hour the call of come and get it echoes
over the swamp and mosquitoes come to find

00:02:10.259 --> 00:02:14.680
the supper. "Come and get it" echoes in the
dark days.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:19.520
Come and get it and the mosquitoes come from
the sinkholes, from pools choked with

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:22.640
grass, weeds, twigs, and flowers.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:27.150
From creeks crowded with water plants, from
all these places mosquitoes come searching

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:32.670
for supper and they come from their hiding
places in hollow tree stumps, from the dark,

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:39.400
cool corners behind them, from the dark cool corners of stables, from the dark cool corners of barns.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:46.769
Yes, evening is suppertime for the malaria
mosquitoes too. They leave the wet places

00:02:46.769 --> 00:02:51.590
where they breed in the dark, cool places
where they hide during the heat of the day,

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:54.659
and they come looking for their supper.

00:02:54.659 --> 00:03:01.659
They come looking for you or somebody like
you looking for people.

00:03:03.329 --> 00:03:09.209
This is the Anopheles quadrimaculatus -- you
can call her quad for short. You can recognize

00:03:09.209 --> 00:03:13.000
her by the way she stands on her head when
she bites.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:20.000
This other mosquito stands hunched up. It's
annoying but it can't give you malaria...but

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:25.939
remember this one, the mosquito that stands
on its head, the malaria mosquito.

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:32.939
She doesn't make much noise and her bite doesn't
sting or hurt much. So the little girl who

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:38.269
was bitten won't say anything about the bite.
Not now.

00:03:38.269 --> 00:03:44.659
But in a few weeks she's sick, call it swamp
fever, chills or ague, but whatever it's called,

00:03:44.659 --> 00:03:51.369
this is malaria. She shivers with cold for
a few hours and then burns with fever.

00:03:51.369 --> 00:04:02.029
[ Background music and singing. Image of young girl in a rocking chair.]

00:04:02.189 --> 00:04:09.049
People who have malaria are so tired and weak
for many months. This is malaria, the malaria

00:04:09.049 --> 00:04:14.840
that passes from the body of the mosquito
to the body of the person when the mosquito bites.

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:21.600
Malaria makes millions sick every year. It
keeps men from work in the fields,

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:24.920
and women from work in the home.

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:30.920
Malaria wears people down and it wears them
out and when a man is rundown, his land runs

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:37.920
down and his home runs down, and his wife
and his children, they run down too.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:46.260
Malaria doesn't kill many but it makes millions
unfit for work, it makes them poor

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:49.200
and it keeps them poor.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:56.130
Here's how malaria gets to people. The little
girl is sick with malaria. She's had no treatment.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:05:01.340
Now a mosquito bites her again and takes some blood from her body, and with her blood takes malaria.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:07.510
The sickness grows in the mosquito's body.
In a few weeks, if that mosquito comes back

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:12.860
to this house and infects one of the family
by biting them, that person will become sick.

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:18.850
A few weeks later he has chills and fever.
The mosquito has taken the malaria from his

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:24.840
sister's blood and put it into his blood.
The farmer looks at both his children

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.540
and worries, and then....

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.680
[Man:] We've got two sick in the house now.

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:33.280
[Woman:] I think we better get a doctor. Better
get him now.

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:39.560
[Man:] Yeah, no use thinking about the money
it'll cost. We can't let them go on like this.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:43.980
And I got to have Jim in the fields. I can't
make out unless I got him helping.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:49.470
[Woman:] Malaria always comes when the crops
need looking after...always stays 'til the

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:53.210
crops are in. And you can't afford to be sick.

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:58.780
[Narrator:] So the doctor comes. He examines
the boy and his sister. Yes, this looks like

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:05.450
malaria, but the doctor makes sure. He takes
a few drops of blood from the finger of each patient.

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:11.060
The blood is smeared on a small piece of glass. Then the blood is examined under the powerful

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:14.880
magnifying glass of a microscope in a laboratory.

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:20.860
This is what the microscope shows; those little
spots in the blood, the spots that are circles,

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:23.940
those are the parasites that cause malaria.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:28.440
Now the doctor is sure and he gives him and
his sister quinine.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:31.580
Sometimes a doctor prescribes atabrine or another medicine.

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:38.380
This medicine destroys the malaria in
their blood and helps them get well

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:43.310
Some people need special treatment. The doctor decides what that treatment should be

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:46.290
and then the doctor speaks to the farmer.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:50.400
[Doctor:] The medicine is going to help them
get well, but if you want to protect your

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:54.360
family against malaria, there are other things
you'll have to do.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:56.650
[Man:] I'll do anything I can, doctor.

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:02.420
[Doctor:] You can start by putting mosquito
netting over both the sickbeds. That's fine.

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:07.840
That net will keep the mosquitoes away from them and then the mosquitoes won't be able

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:10.730
to bite them and carry the malaria to somebody else.

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:14.560
[Woman:] For how long, doctor? How long are
they going to be sick?

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:20.300
[Doctor:] They'll start getting better soon.
Malaria doesn't bother people long if they

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:24.160
get the right kind of treatment. They should
be up and around in a few days.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.880
Of course, they'll have to continue treatment.

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:29.640
[Woman:] Is there anything more I can do,
Doctor?

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:34.140
[Doctor:] Give them the medicine in the way I told you and keep them as comfortable as you can.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:40.040
But there's a lot you can do to prevent
malaria. The man who can help you do it is

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:44.660
your health officer. Better look him up the first chance you get.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:49.090
[Narrator:] And a week or so later the health
officer comes to the house and tells the farmer

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:52.000
what he can do to protect his family against
malaria.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:57.670
[Health officer:] You've got to screen this
porch. And use fine wire so malaria mosquitos

00:07:57.670 --> 00:08:03.130
can't get through it. All the windows should be screened. The way to keep malaria out is to

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:09.860
keep mosquitoes out. Every opening big enough
to let a mosquito in must be covered or screened.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:14.840
[Man:] It's kinda hard to put out a lot of
money for screens this time of year.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:19.280
[Health officer:] It doesn't cost a lot of
money. It might be a lot to put out at one time, but it only

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:23.890
comes to about three dollars a year. Most
of you folks are spending about twenty-five

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:29.450
dollars every year for pill medicines. It's
a lot cheaper to buy screens.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:33.820
[Man:] I guess it is. Still money is right
scarce this time of year.

00:08:33.829 --> 00:08:38.869
[Health officer:] If you folks are really
poor, you might borrow it. You've got to protect your family.

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:42.220
When you get the screening, I'll show you how to put it up and even if the

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:44.740
screening is up you've got a job to do.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:51.580
You've got to look for mosquitoes in all the
dark, cool corners where they hide. Look behind

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:56.280
the bed and in the dark, cool places in the
barn.

00:08:56.680 --> 00:09:02.180
Wherever there's a dark, cool place, because that's where mosquitoes hide,

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:07.440
and when you find mosquitoes, you've got to swat them or kill them with a spray gun.

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:11.990
[Narrator:] Those are the things you can do
to fight malaria to keep yourself and your

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:18.990
family healthy and at work. Keep the mosquitoes
out, but there's more to be done.

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:25.190
The mosquitoes must be destroyed. That is
your community's job. Malaria mosquitoes lay

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:31.870
their eggs in warm pools and ponds near the
banks of quiet lakes, near water plants.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:38.220
Ponds can be drained so that the mosquitoes
will have no place to lay their eggs. Sometimes

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:42.800
ponds can be filled to destroy the breeding
places of the malaria mosquito.

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:49.140
These are the larvae or wiggle-tails that
hatch out of the malaria mosquito egg.

00:09:49.140 --> 00:09:54.480
Brush at the water's edge makes a protective place for the larvae. When the brush is cut away,

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:57.360
this protection is destroyed.

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:02.930
The wiggle-tails live in water until they become full-grown mosquitoes.

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:05.820
 Poison dust spread on the water kills the wiggle-tails.

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:09.750
Oils sprayed on the surface of the water kill
the wiggle- tails too.

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:16.310
In some places, planes are used to spray water
with poison dust. All these things have to

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:20.640
be done by people who know how, people trained
to do the work.

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:27.640
It's a big job. It takes a long time and costs
a lot of money, but it doesn't cost as much

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:33.510
as malaria costs, and it prevents the sickness and suffering that malaria brings.

00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:39.140
The community must get rid of malaria mosquitoes
for good with dust and oil, with permanent

00:10:39.140 --> 00:10:44.960
draining systems that leave no quiet water
in which these mosquitoes can lay their eggs.

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:50.860
But until the community does this, you have
a job to do in your home, your church,

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:54.880
your meeting halls. You've got to keep mosquitoes out.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:11:00.480
Screen the doors and windows, cover the
fireplaces to keep them from coming down through

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:07.380
the chimney. Cover the cracks in the floor.
Cover the cracks in the walls and ceiling.

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:10.250
Those things are your job.

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:15.510
If you need help, speak to your health officer.
He can tell you how to keep mosquitoes and

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:20.220
malaria out of your house, how to protect
your home and family.

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:25.260
Fight malaria so that you can be strong to
do the work that must be done. 

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:35.100
Strong to live well so that when evening time comes, resting time, you can rest safely.

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:41.080
Remember the mosquito that stands on her head
can put you flat on your back.

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:47.200
Ask your health officer for advice. Keep the mosquitoes out. Keep malaria out.

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:58.040
[Organ music]

